{"availability":"available","full":"rust-js-lang/rust-js","name":"rust-js","description":"Compile Rust to readable JavaScript. Built on rustc, inspired by Scala.js & ReScript","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T13:18:52Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:51:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rust-js-lang.github.io/rust-js/","topics":[],"demo":"https://rust-js-lang.github.io/rust-js/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.779Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.779Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.779Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.779Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I thought it would be great if I could do UI programming—my day job—in Rust.","Rust gives us a powerful way to describe programs and catch mistakes before they run. JavaScript gives us the runtime and ecosystem in which much of our software already lives: browsers, React, npm packages, and tools such as Vite and Bun.","We want to use them together. Write a React component in Rust, import a JavaScript package, call a browser API, and inspect the result in DevTools. Let Rust check the program and let JavaScript run it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rust-js-lang/rust-js/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"aae57838e57516fff7f7fea89c9586e80ead9837fc34eb3e58fac09b03e3b356","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.928Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.928Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"I thought it would be great if I could do UI programming—my day job—in Rust.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rust-js-lang/rust-js/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"aae57838e57516fff7f7fea89c9586e80ead9837fc34eb3e58fac09b03e3b356","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rust-js-lang/rust-js/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:25.928Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated"